    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>Countdown Timer for Gutenberg Block Editor helps you build urgency-driven sections for launches, discounts, promos, events, and evergreen campaigns.</p>\n<p>Features include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>fixed-date mode</li>\n<li>evergreen visitor-based mode</li>\n<li>expiry actions such as message, hide, or redirect</li>\n<li>unit toggles for days, hours, minutes, and seconds</li>\n<li>editable labels and style presets</li>\n<li>broad layout and styling controls</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Developer Credits</h3>\n<p>This plugin was developed by ConicPlex, a leading agency specializing in WordPress plugin development. For more information about ConicPlex and their services, visit <a href=\"https://conicplex.com\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">ConicPlex</a>.</p>\n<h3>Credits &amp; 3rd Party Services</h3>\n<p><strong><a href=\"https://conicplex.com/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">ConicPlex.com</a></strong>: Countdown Timer for Block Editor uses <a href=\"https://conicplex.com/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">ConicPlex</a> (own website) to store plugin insights. Whenever the plugin is activated, deactivated, or uninstalled, an API request is sent to Conicplex to record the action. The API request includes the action, site URL, admin email, plugin version, plugin name, plugin text domain, WordPress version, site language, and site timezone. <a href=\"https://conicplex.com/privacy-policy/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Privacy Policy</a>, <a href=\"https://conicplex.com/terms-conditions/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Terms &amp; Conditions</a>.</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the plugin folder to <code>/wp-content/plugins/</code>.</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin through the WordPress admin.</li>\n<li>Insert the <code>Countdown Timer</code> block in the block editor.</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id=\"does%20evergreen%20mode%20depend%20on%20an%20external%20service%3F\">\nDoes evergreen mode depend on an external service?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>No. Evergreen countdown behavior is handled locally in the browser.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id=\"can%20i%20redirect%20users%20after%20expiry%3F\">\nCan I redirect users after expiry?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes. The block supports redirect as one of the expiry actions.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.0.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial release.</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "Add fixed-date and evergreen countdown timers to the WordPress block editor.",
    "description": "<p>Countdown Timer for Gutenberg Block Editor helps you build urgency-driven sections for launches, discounts, promos, events, and evergreen campaigns.</p>\n<p>Features include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>fixed-date mode</li>\n<li>evergreen visitor-based mode</li>\n<li>expiry actions such as message, hide, or redirect</li>\n<li>unit toggles for days, hours, minutes, and seconds</li>\n<li>editable labels and style presets</li>\n<li>broad layout and styling controls</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Developer Credits</h3>\n<p>This plugin was developed by ConicPlex, a leading agency specializing in WordPress plugin development. For more information about ConicPlex and their services, visit <a href=\"https://conicplex.com\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">ConicPlex</a>.</p>\n<h3>Credits &amp; 3rd Party Services</h3>\n<p><strong><a href=\"https://conicplex.com/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">ConicPlex.com</a></strong>: Countdown Timer for Block Editor uses <a href=\"https://conicplex.com/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">ConicPlex</a> (own website) to store plugin insights. Whenever the plugin is activated, deactivated, or uninstalled, an API request is sent to Conicplex to record the action. The API request includes the action, site URL, admin email, plugin version, plugin name, plugin text domain, WordPress version, site language, and site timezone. <a href=\"https://conicplex.com/privacy-policy/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Privacy Policy</a>, <a href=\"https://conicplex.com/terms-conditions/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Terms &amp; Conditions</a>.</p>\n",
